# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR MIT
#
# What the kernel stage asserts about the built kernel.
#
#   y SYMBOL      CONFIG_SYMBOL is switched on (=y) after `make olddefconfig`;
#                 kernel.sh also enables it on top of the base config, so a
#                 symbol that a config cleanup dropped is put back
#   m SYMBOL      CONFIG_SYMBOL is built as a module (=m); a =y here means
#                 something selects it built in, which is a finding, not a nit
#   line TEXT     this exact line is in .config (integers, strings and
#                 "is not set" lines, which the y/m checks cannot express)
#   file NAME.ko  the module is installed under lib/modules after
#                 modules_install; a Kconfig symbol does not carry its object
#                 name, so the names are listed and this list keeps both honest
#
# Why asserted and not trusted: olddefconfig silently drops a symbol whose
# dependencies are unmet, and a defconfig is minimal (savedefconfig omits every
# symbol at its default), so the config file alone cannot show that a symbol the
# board needs is still on.
#
line CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT=10
line # CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM is not set
line CONFIG_DRM_CLIENT_DEFAULT="fbdev"
line CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=256
y SECURITY_DMESG_RESTRICT
y DYNAMIC_DEBUG
y FTRACE
y ENABLE_DEFAULT_TRACERS
y DEBUG_FS
